| **09-01** | ✅🔴 **OpenAI — JALAPEÑO PRESENTATION AT HOT CHIPS (COMPANY PRIMARY, presented 2026-08-25; transcribed quotes via Tae Kim / Key Context, 2026-09-01)** | **produto / competicao** | **bull for AVGO, and it RETIRES a flag** | ★★ **THE PRIMARY SOURCE THAT CLOSES THE "NINE MONTHS" QUESTION FOR GOOD. Richard Ho (VP of Hardware, ex-Google TPU): *"The Jalapeño chip. It is here. It's real. We have the systems in the lab… **We did basically the entire RTL EXECUTION in nine months.**"* And in Q&A, asked how much was existing Broadcom IP: *"**Most of the chip is designed from scratch.** The compute die I think only has like some interface IP and there's an IO chip… **a lot of the interfaces are existing IP, the rest of it was all like fresh RTL in XLS plus and Verilog.**"* ➤ ✅ **So the nine months is RTL EXECUTION, not concept-to-tape-out — which reconciles cleanly with this page's dated ~16-month design-to-tape-out sequence AND with SemiAnalysis's A0-silicon-nine-months-after-a-November-2025-CoWoS-tape-out framing. The flag raised on 08-31 is now retired against a primary source rather than a relay.** 🔴 **AND AVGO IS NAMED ON THE RECORD, ALONGSIDE A SECOND PARTNER THIS PAGE HAD NOT LINKED TO JALAPEÑO: *"I also want to give a really big shout out to our partners, **BROADCOM and CELESTICA**, who are very key partners for us to be able to deliver this capability here."*** **FORWARD: *"This is **step one of a multi-generational roadmap. We have GENERATION TWO already well under development, and we're heading towards TAPEOUT in some number of months.**"* ➤ **A gen-2 tape-out "in some number of months" is the single most concrete forward AVGO-revenue signal in this window and it comes from the customer, not the vendor.** **TECHNICAL, for the competitive file: memory-sliced architecture (*"every core has a local view of its own HBM slice"*); a purpose-built collective network between cores; chose good-at-decode-AND-prefill over a decode-only chip *"preserving locality"*; **scale-up ETHERNET protocol at 200 gigabit** (not NVLink); standard-cell methodology, no custom cells; **1.7GHz in the lab vs a 1.8GHz POR** (*"sandbagged a little bit"*). Performance claims: *"almost **1500 tokens per second per user**"* on OSS at *"4x less latency"* for today's highest throughput; **700 tok/s/user on DeepSeek at 5x lower latency**; *"**the larger the model, the larger the advantage**"*; and *"HBM is not the bottleneck."* |
| **08-31** | **AVGO — VMware Explore 2026 (COMPANY PRIMARY, 3-day event, Las Vegas)** | **produto / competicao** | **mixed** | 🔴 **THE ONE THAT CUTS AGAINST THE NVDA RELATIONSHIP: *"AVGO VMware announced own version of an '**AI factory**' à la [[NVDA]] that **uses [[AMD]] Instinct GPUs and the open AMD ROCm software ecosystem.** Per management, VMware AI Factory is an '**evolution**' of VMware Private AI Foundation with NVDA"* (The Register, via MS desk · Tom Wigg, 2026-09-01). Other announcements: *"VMware Cloud Foundation Brings Leading AI Models to the Private AI Cloud"*, *"Broadcom Strengthens Spring Security and Adds Coverage of Java, Python, and Node Ecosystems with TrueSource"*, *"Broadcom Unveils AI-Ready Data Foundations"* (@StockMKTNewz, 08-31). ➤ **A Broadcom software product whose flagship AI reference architecture runs AMD silicon is a small but real datapoint on where AVGO sees the merchant-GPU market going — and it lands the same week JPM calls custom and merchant *"complementary, not substitutive."*** |
| **08-31** | **@BenBajarin (corpus)** ⚠️ *independent analyst, not a broker* | **competicao** | **bear (long-dated)** | *"After digesting, and having a few background call backs on the [[NVDA]]-[[MEDIATEK]] deal, **while the short term impact to AVGO is not threatened, I do think you have to seriously weigh the LONGER TERM impact on their custom XPU business. Others are going to get more volume than originally assumed.**"* ✅ **Same conclusion from a second corpus account (@aleabitoreddit): NVDA is *"playing kingmaker with the next generation of ASIC winners like [[MRVL]] / MediaTek, with a **second order effect of eroding AVGO position**. Playbook feels similar to what they did with Neoclouds like [[NBIS]] and [[CRWV]] — help create the next leaders, then make them both financially and strategically aligned with Nvidia."*** ➤ **Note this is the SAME concern JPM's buy-side survey prices — respondents 5% below consensus on F28 AI revenue. The narrative and the numbers now agree.** |
