🔴🔴 **THE BUYSIDE IS POSITIONED *BELOW* CONSENSUS ON FY28 AI — THE OPPOSITE OF THE "CROWDED LONG WITH AN IMPOSSIBLE BAR" FRAMING: *"respondents to my buyside survey are **5% below consensus for F28 AI revenue**, underscoring lingering questions from you all about AVGO's future GOOGL projects."*** ➜ **Read against the near-term survey, which is ABOVE the Street — consensus models revenue **+33% q/q & +85% y/y**, the buyside survey **+36% & +89%**, *"all backed by over 150% YoY growth in AI revenue"*, with an expected **2.2% revenue beat** (*"wider than we've recently seen"*, against a company whose *"beats of consensus historically tend to be modest"*). **The bar is high on the QUARTER and low on the OUT-YEAR. That is a specific, tradeable shape, and it is the cleanest statement of the setup on this page.**
🔴 **THE RAISE THE BUYSIDE IS UNDERWRITING, WHICH IS THE NUMBER TO SCORE THE PRINT AGAINST: *"The majority of respondents also expect Hock to raise the FY27 AI revenue guide, with **$120bn the clear consensus landing zone** - though several respondents pushed for **$130bn**, and a few expect only a qualitative upgrade."*** ➜ ⚠️⚠️ **PUT THE FOUR BARS SIDE BY SIDE, BECAUSE THEY DO NOT AGREE AND THE SPREAD *IS* THE RISK: buyside landing zone **$120bn** (JPM survey) · MS/Moore house estimate **~$120bn** with *"some expectations assume more than $150bn"* · Jefferies/Curtis *"expectations are already in the $130-140bn range"* · JPM/Sur house model **$130bn+**. A single print cannot clear a bar that is quoted anywhere from $120bn to $150bn — which is precisely why last quarter's beat-and-raise sold off.**
**POSITIONING, and it is NOT maximally crowded: *"Broadcom remains a quite crowded net long — helped over the past few weeks by short covering into earnings — but thanks to a greater willingness among investors to be short the name (likely for funding purposes), **net crowding is not as extended as it has been recently, and somewhat trails blue-chip tech peers including [[NVDA]]**."* **Positioning score +3 on a −5/+5 scale. Implied move 6.3%.** **Print: Sept 2, ~4:15pm ET release, 5pm call.**
