| **08-20** | 🔴 **BofA Asia semis + components conference call — BofA Asia tech team, host "Robert", semis analyst rendered "Haas", components "Doris". BROKER-HOSTED CALL, not a published note: no AVGO rating, PT or estimate. Feedback from BofA's Asia tech tour plus earnings season; ASR spelling noise ("L-Chip"=Alchip).** | **competicao / demanda** | **mixed** | 🔴 **THE COMPETITIVE ITEM, AND IT MOVES THE GOOGLE DEBATE FORWARD TWO GENERATIONS: BofA reports a LIVE investor debate over whether [[AMD]], BROADCOM, ALCHIP or GUC penetrates the [[GOOG]] TPU supply chain ABOUT TWO YEARS OUT — i.e. at TPU V10.** ⚠️ **The counter-evidence BofA supplies against a new entrant is incumbency at the integration layer, and it does not favour Broadcom either: MediaTek's own feedback is that it has been on V10's "TRIPLET" architecture with Google SINCE 2H LAST YEAR and DOES THE INTEGRATION.** ➜ **Carry both readings. CONSTRUCTIVE: Broadcom is still named as a candidate at V10, two generations past the v9 order loss this page has been trading — the incumbency is not conceded, which is the forward extension of MS/Moore's "In Defense of AVGO's ~80% ASIC share." UNCOMFORTABLE: AVGO is now one of FOUR names in a contest at a customer where it was the default, and the party with the dated architectural head start is neither Broadcom nor the challengers but MediaTek.** ⚠️ **Do NOT harden "V10" into a design-win or a share number — BofA frames it as a debate about ~two years out, and the MediaTek/[[GOOG]] specifics belong on those pages.** **Design-services preference, for the competitive set: investors like MediaTek, GUC and Alchip; ALCHIP IS LEAST PREFERRED on communication track record; BofA prefers AI over non-AI (contrasted with UMC).** **THE DEMAND BACKDROP, which is constructive and matters to the FY27 debate on this page: GPU and CPU demand is *"trending better as compared to people's expectation ahead of the earnings season back in early July"* — better on yield, mass-production schedule and technology development — with the supply side showing *"pretty nice progress across foundries, back end packaging and testing partners, as well as the equipment players."* **Hyperscaler capex still trending UP: companies on the tour *"are not seeing any of the slowdown from hyperscaler investment despite the fact that there has been some news talking about [[GOOG]] as well as [[META]] might slowing down their investment or cutting their head count in the frontier model development"*; growth may moderate but *"AI investment is still going to be leading the semiconductor growth."*** 🔴 **AND THE MECHANISM, WHICH IS THE MOST DIRECTLY BULLISH PASSAGE FOR AN ASIC FRANCHISE ANYONE HAS PUBLISHED THIS MONTH: into 2H26 and 2027 *"we are going to see more of the adoption on the ASICs as well as GPUs because hyperscalers are going to spend every single piece of their money in a more disciplined way… more cost effective as well. Just because the component cost especially in memory is just getting higher, while they will not be able to fully fulfil their own capex with their free cash flow as well as cash position as compared with one to two years ago. So that does mean **they will need to either raise more capital externally, which will force them to be thinking about the monetization of AI models instead of continuing to make a huge investment on GPUs for the frontier model training**."*** ➜ **Memory-cost inflation plus a funding constraint is exactly the argument for merchant-GPU-to-custom-ASIC substitution and for inference over frontier training — the demand-side case for AVGO's book, arriving from the same call that puts its Google incumbency into a four-way contest at V10.** **Supply items from the same call, cross-filed [[TSM]]: TSMC is running out of space for CoWoS-R packaging for CPU and is indirectly outsourcing that business to ASE; merchant CPU supply is getting tighter into 2027; and new ASIC projects are *"picking up strongly from the front end manufacturing perspective and then will be through the back end packaging, the CoWoS packaging pretty soon from fourth quarter this year"* to support TPU volume doubling in 2027.** (BofA Asia semis + components call, 2026-08-20) [Source](../relat%C3%B3rios%20bons/2026_08_20_baml_call.html) |
