| 07-27 | UBS · Timothy Arcuri ("SemiBytes: GOOGL Capex, NVDA and AVGO") | competicao | bull | **Two AVGO-relevant reads.** (1) On the Samsung MoU (**$200B+ over 5 years to ~C2030, memory + foundry**): UBS reads it as **AVGO securing memory supply AND potentially reducing its reliance on TSMC**, since the agreement gives AVGO access to **Samsung's 2nm foundry process, HBM, and advanced packaging** — with the packaging leg **added to AVGO's own Singapore facility**. (2) On the Google share debate, UBS argues **investors have become too negative on the Google situation**: Google's decision to go with a **chiplet design for v8t de-risks AVGO's ability to ramp versus MediaTek**, which is heavily reliant on **INTC's EMIB-T process — a process UBS thinks still suffers from very low yields and immaturity**. A direct technical rebuttal to the MediaTek share-cede thread (Bear items 10-12) on execution-risk grounds rather than share math. Framing context: UBS lifts its hyperscaler capex framework to **$1.34T in 2027E / $1.48T in 2028E** (+43%/+11% vs prior), with the big-4 >70% of industry spend. (UBS · Timothy Arcuri, 2026-07-27) |
