| **08-18** | 🔴🔴 **Wells Fargo · Aaron Rakers (w/ Michael Tsvetanov, Richard Strifler) — "F3Q26 Preview: AI Semi Upside & Custom XPU Competition Remain Key Focus." OVERWEIGHT, PT $545** (px $392.43) — **net-new house on this page** | **guidance / demanda** | **bull (Street-high FY27)** | ★ **THE HIGHEST FY27 AI NUMBER ON THIS PAGE, AND IT IS A $/GW ASSUMPTION MORE THAN A GW ASSUMPTION.** FY27 AI semi **$141.5bn vs Street $118.8bn (+19%)**; FY28 **$205.3bn vs $168.2bn (+22%)**; FY27/FY28 EPS **$21.70 / $29.00 vs Street $19.45 / $26.18**. **F3Q26 itself modelled in line** (rev $29.449bn vs $29.479bn; AI semis $16.037bn vs $16.110bn; EPS $3.22 vs $3.24) — **the entire disagreement is the out-years.** Method is **GWs deployed × $B/GW**, explicitly rejecting units × ASP: FY27 **7.581GW at a blended $13.5bn/GW** (Google 7.00GW @$14.5 · Anthropic 2.50 @$14.5 · Meta MTIA 1.00 @$12.0 · OpenAI 1.35 @$12.2 · other 0.425 @$10.5), to **$247.5bn AI semi revenue by FY29**. ⚠️ **Wells' own note concedes Epoch AI data implies ~$11bn/GW (TPU v7 ≈ $11,740/chip) against management's $10–20bn band — at Epoch's number the same GW ladder lands BELOW consensus. Stress the $/GW, not the GW.** **Net-new disclosures: RPO $164.6bn exiting F2Q26 (~30% recognised NTM) with the 10-Q newly citing a long-term contract (singular, read as Google) for custom AI ASICs entered in F3Q26; purchase commitments $128.1bn ($55.2bn FY27 / $72.9bn FY28); inventory $4.328bn.** ⚠️ **The note's base-period comparatives ($54m F1Q26 purchase commitments; $45.0bn F1Q26 RPO) imply implausible sequential steps and are NOT adopted — levels carried, comparatives flagged pending the 10-Q.** Also: **Tomahawk 6 packaging PULLED IN to August from December** at the new Singapore fab; **WT Micro (~42% of F2Q26 semi sales, R²=0.97) July-quarter NT$562.6bn +139% y/y but 3Q26 guided roughly FLAT q/q — Wells reads F3Q26 as broadly in line, with the acceleration in 4Q26 and 2027.** |
